ual  money well but because you know from the  the way the housing system works uh  and there's a whole other argument to be  had about planning  um but the way the housing system works  it just means you are when you're alive  you have a lot more wealth and a lot  more asset just because  the same house in different parts of the  country is worth different things now  to solve that requires a lot of change  about planning and indeed leveling up so  that  uh house prices go up in other parts of  the country because they become  uh in places where people want to move  to uh but that's that's a longer term  thing  in the meantime what what you can do now  is to say wherever you are in the  country  you get to keep the same percentage of  your assets  so that you will know you know roughly  what your house is worth and therefore  if you're thinking about you know what  can i leave uh to my children  then you will know that you've got the  the bulk of that  uh to leave um you've been in number 10  for quite some time as deputy prime  minister you were  a minister in other departments has the  prime minister made the right judgment  today uh  to work from number 10 under this pilot  scheme to which  it appears every cabinet minister has  access  and hardly anybody else does well it's  not  clear who's got access to it but yeah i  mean i think the  in practical terms allowing the prime  minister and the chancellor of exchequer  to work as normally as possible  is actually quite sensible and and i  hope one of the effects of this  is to accelerate the  the pilot scheme and indeed the analysis  of the pilot scheme because this might  be  a way out of the current problems of  people not being able to  uh go to work i think the sooner we get  to that uh the better and and clearly  daily testing is one way to achieve that  so i  you know i'd be very keen if we could  move to a system where  uh if you if you have been in contact  with someone um but you're showing no  symptoms 